\title{cfomics: Comparing, Selecting and Combining CATE Estimators for Omics Data}
\description{
A unified workflow for estimating conditional average treatment effects (CATE) in high-dimensional omics data, where the sample size is much smaller than the number of features and no single estimator is reliably best in advance. The package fits many CATE estimators behind one interface and compares them on a data-only loss, selects the best, or combines them into an ensemble, so that an analysis does not hinge on an arbitrary choice of method. SummarizedExperiment and MultiAssayExperiment inputs are supported directly, and the estimated individual effects can be written back onto these objects for downstream differential-expression and pathway analyses. Both R-native estimators and Python backends (provisioned automatically through basilisk) are included.
}
